  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **intro music (I'd Really Love To See You Tonight)**: back after 107 archived shows (1529 days); rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Shirtless in Hamburg**: rare: 10 archived performances [2]\n- **(banter, seen from space)**: back after 72 archived shows (764 days) [2]\n- **(banter, noteboook retrieval)**: back after 72 archived shows (764 days) [2]\n- **The House That Dripped Blood**: rare: 7 archived performances [2]\n- **(requests, let the man call an audible)**: back after 72 archived shows (764 days) [2]\n- **(banter, pro wrestling)**: back after 72 archived shows (764 days) [2]\n- **(banter, oldest one on the list)**: back after 72 archived shows (764 days) [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2024-01-21** (recommended): source not stated; 31 songs; 90 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Guests: I Hope You Dance intro [1]\n- Show was a John Darnielle and Matt Douglas duo performance, fourth date of the 2024 Sworn To The Effort duo tour [1]\n- Bully and Craig Finn played the opening slots before the duo [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2024-01-21**: taped by astrolyric; transferred by astrolyric; source: PCM-A10 (onboard mics, placed above crowd level on right side of the stage) [1]. Also: Taper says this is their first finished and uploaded tape, after earlier taping attempts; they recorded without openly having permission [1]",
